From: Runeon Contributors <dev@runeon.com>
Subject: [PATCH] server: warn once when the msync node pool runs out

A downstream msync fix, not a WineHQ backport: WineHQ has no msync.
Runs only when WINEMSYNC is set.

Once the 0x80000-node pool is empty, every wait registration allocates
a node with malloc() and wrote the same warning to stderr, which is
unbuffered: one write per registration on the thread that serves all
msync waits. 120 processes exiting with 100 threads each in an alertable
wait for 63 events wrote 243757 such lines in one session. Write the
warning once per wineserver; the fallback allocation is unchanged.

--- a/server/msync.c
+++ b/server/msync.c
@@ -177,7 +177,15 @@
 {
     if (pool->count == 0)
     {
-        fprintf( stderr, "msync: warn: node memory pool exhausted\n" );
+        static int warned;
+
+        /* stderr is unbuffered: a line for every allocation past the pool
+         * stalls the message pump once it runs out, so warn only once */
+        if (!warned)
+        {
+            fprintf( stderr, "msync: warn: node memory pool exhausted\n" );
+            warned = 1;
+        }
         return malloc( sizeof(struct tid_node) );
     }
     return pool->free_nodes[--pool->count];
